Article 1 Where, without permission of the owner of a registered trademark, a person uses a trademark identical to the registered trademark on the same kind of goods, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be considered as "serious circumstances" under Article 213 of the Criminal Law, and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and/or shall be fined:
(1) The illegal business turnover is not less than 50,000 yuan or the illegal gains are not less than 30,000 yuan;
(2) Counterfeiting two or more registered trademarks, with an illegal business turnover of not less than 30,000 yuan or illegal gains of not less than 20,000 yuan;
(3) Other circumstances that are serious.
Where any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be considered as "particularly serious circumstances" under Article 213 of the Criminal Law, and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) The illegal business turnover is not less than 250,000 yuan or the illegal gains are not less than 150,000 yuan;
(2) Counterfeiting two or more registered trademarks, with an illegal business turnover of not less than 150,000 yuan or illegal gains of not less than 100,000 yuan;
(3) Other circumstances that are particularly serious.

Article 3: Counterfeiting or manufacturing without authorization another person's registered trademark labels, or selling counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured registered trademark labels, which falls under any of the following circumstances, shall constitute "serious circumstances" as stipulated in Article 215 of the Criminal Law, and the perpetrator shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention or public surveillance, and shall also, or shall only, be fined for the crime of illegally manufacturing or selling illegally manufactured registered trademark labels:
(1) The number of counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured or sold counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured registered trademark labels reaches 20,000 or more, or the illegal business turnover amounts to 50,000 yuan or more, or the illegal gains amount to 30,000 yuan or more;
(2) The number of counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured or sold counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured registered trademark labels of two or more types reaches 10,000 or more, or the illegal business turnover amounts to 30,000 yuan or more, or the illegal gains amount to 20,000 yuan or more;
(3) Other circumstances where the circumstances are serious.

Where it falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall constitute "especially serious circumstances" as stipulated in Article 215 of the Criminal Law, and the perpetrator shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years, and shall also be fined for the crime of illegally manufacturing or selling illegally manufactured registered trademark labels:
(1) The number of counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured or sold counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured registered trademark labels reaches 100,000 or more, or the illegal business turnover amounts to 250,000 yuan or more, or the illegal gains amount to 150,000 yuan or more;
(2) The number of counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured or sold counterfeit or unauthorized manufactured registered trademark labels of two or more types reaches 50,000 or more, or the illegal business turnover amounts to 150,000 yuan or more, or the illegal gains amount to 100,000 yuan or more;
(3) Other circumstances where the circumstances are especially serious.

Article 4 Where a person counterfeits another person's patent, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be considered as "serious circumstances" under Article 216 of the Criminal Law, and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and/or shall be fined:
(1) The illegal business turnover is not less than 200,000 yuan or the illegal gains are not less than 100,000 yuan;
(2) Causing direct economic losses of not less than 500,000 yuan to the patentee;
(3) Counterfeiting two or more of another person's patents, with an illegal business turnover of not less than 100,000 yuan or illegal gains of not less than 50,000 yuan;
(4) Other circumstances that are serious.

Article 5 Where, for the purpose of profit, a person commits any of the acts of copyright infringement listed in Article 217 of the Criminal Law, and the illegal gains are not less than 30,000 yuan, it shall be considered as "a relatively large amount of illegal gains"; where any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be considered as "other serious circumstances", and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and/or shall be fined:
(1) The illegal business turnover is not less than 50,000 yuan;
(2) Without permission of the copyright owner, reproducing and distributing his written works, music, films, television programs, video recordings, computer software, or other works, with the total number of reproductions not less than 1,000 copies (pieces);
(3) Other circumstances that are serious.
Where, for the purpose of profit, a person commits any of the acts of copyright infringement listed in Article 217 of the Criminal Law, and the illegal gains are not less than 150,000 yuan, it shall be considered as "a huge amount of illegal gains"; where any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be considered as "other particularly serious circumstances", and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) The illegal business turnover is not less than 250,000 yuan;
(2) Without permission of the copyright owner, reproducing and distributing his written works, music, films, television programs, video recordings, computer software, or other works, with the total number of reproductions not less than 5,000 copies (pieces);
(3) Other circumstances that are particularly serious.

Article 9 The "sales amount" as provided in Article 214 of the Criminal Law refers to all illegal income obtained and receivable after selling goods bearing a counterfeit registered trademark.
Any of the following circumstances shall be deemed as "knowingly" under Article 214 of the Criminal Law:
(1) The person knows that the registered trademark on the goods he sells has been altered, replaced, or covered;
(2) The person has previously received an administrative penalty or has assumed civil liability for selling goods bearing a counterfeit registered trademark, and again sells the same kind of goods bearing a counterfeit registered trademark;
(3) The person forges or alters the authorization document of the trademark registrant, or knows that such document has been forged or altered;
(4) Other circumstances where the person knows or should know that the goods bear a counterfeit registered trademark.

Article 10 Any of the following acts shall constitute the act of "counterfeiting another person's patent" under Article 216 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Without permission, marking another person's patent number on the goods manufactured or sold by the actor or on the packaging of such goods;
(2) Without permission, using another person's patent number in advertisements or other promotional materials, causing people to mistake the technology involved for another person's patented technology;
(3) Without permission, using another person's patent number in a contract, causing people to mistake the technology involved in the contract for another person's patented technology;
(4) Forging or altering another person's patent certificate, patent documents, or patent application documents.
